# The Kauffman iterant, the discrete origin of the imaginary unit. An iterant is a period-two oscillation read together
# with the shift that advances it, and the imaginary unit is what that structure becomes: not an added axiom but the
# generator of a four-step cycle. This file MODELS that cycle as the group of fourth roots of unity, the four values one,
# i, minus one and minus i, and DEFINES the act of multiplying by i as a function stepping around them. It then PROVES the
# laws that make i the imaginary unit: multiplying by i has order four, four steps return every value to itself, while two
# steps send one to minus one, so i squared is minus one. Complex conjugation, sending i to minus i, is shown to be three
# steps of the same shift, i cubed, and to be an involution. Every theorem is quantified over the actual four-element type
# and checked by induction, so this is the imaginary unit built from a discrete distinction, the iterant made a group.

# The four fourth roots of unity, the elements of the cyclic group the iterant generates.
form iterant
  case one
  case eye
  case minus-one
  case minus-eye

# Multiplying by i: the shift that steps one to i to minus one to minus i and back to one. This one function is the whole
# iterant, the oscillation and its advance together.
task times-i
  take a, like iterant
  like iterant
  fork case, read a
    case one
      send back
        make eye
    case eye
      send back
        make minus-one
    case minus-one
      send back
        make minus-eye
    case minus-eye
      send back
        make one

# Complex conjugation, sending i to minus i and fixing the reals.
task flip
  take a, like iterant
  like iterant
  fork case, read a
    case one
      send back
        make one
    case eye
      send back
        make minus-eye
    case minus-one
      send back
        make minus-one
    case minus-eye
      send back
        make eye

# I SQUARED IS MINUS ONE: two steps of the shift send one to minus one, the defining relation of the imaginary unit,
# here a computed fact about the shift, not an assumption.
rule i-squared-is-minus-one
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call times-i
        call times-i
          make one
      make minus-one
  calm hold

# ORDER FOUR: four steps of the shift return EVERY value to itself, times-i applied four times is the identity, for all a.
# So multiplying by i has order four and the four roots form the cyclic group of order four. Proved by induction over the
# four elements.
rule multiplying-by-i-has-order-four
  seat a, like iterant
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call times-i
        call times-i
          call times-i
            call times-i
              read a
      read a
  fold a

# CONJUGATION REVERSES THE SHIFT: conjugation is an anti-automorphism, turning multiplication by i into multiplication by
# its inverse. Conjugating after one shift equals three shifts after conjugating, flip (times-i a) = times-i (times-i
# (times-i (flip a))), for every a. So conjugation sends i to minus i not by rotating but by reversing the direction of
# the shift, the iterant read backward. Proved by induction over the four elements.
rule conjugation-reverses-the-shift
  seat a, like iterant
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call flip
        call times-i
          read a
      call times-i
        call times-i
          call times-i
            call flip
              read a
  fold a

# CONJUGATION IS AN INVOLUTION: conjugating twice returns the value, flip (flip a) = a, for every a, so conjugation is its
# own inverse, the reflection that squares to the identity.
rule conjugation-is-an-involution
  seat a, like iterant
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call flip
        call flip
          read a
      read a
  fold a
